  "title": "Chunky Guacamole",
  "description": "Guacamole can be served not only with tortilla chips, but also with fresh sliced vegetables, such as radishes, cucumber, or celery.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The secret to perfect guacamole is ripe avocados. If you prefer a smoother guacamole, use a blender. Personally, I prefer avocados crushed with a fork with&nbsp;finely cut tomatoes, onions, and cilantro.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21591,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1659208511846} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21591-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Chunky Guacamole</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9564.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tGuacamole can be served not only with tortilla chips, but also with fresh sliced vegetables, such as radishes, cucumber, or celery.\r\n\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>3 ripe avocados</li><li>1/2 lemon (or lime)</li><li>2 small tomatoes</li><li>1/2 oignon</li><li>2 cloves clove garlic</li><li>Salt and freshly ground black pepper</li><li>1-2 pinches cayenne pepper (or chili powder)</li><li>Fresh cilantro</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Slice the avocados in half along its length and dispose of the seed and skin. Crush the flesh of the avocado using a fork. Drizzle with the lemon juice.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9555.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Chop the onions, tomatoes, and cilantro. Crush the garlic.<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9557.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Mix all the vegetables and avocados together. Salt, pepper, and add the cayenne pepper.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9558.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Put the guacamole in a bowl and serve along with tortilla chips or sliced vegetables.\r\n<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/05/IMG_9559.Blog_-1-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Appetizers</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
